{"type":"compaction","id":"6d5b0eb7","parentId":"49c8dda6","timestamp":"2026-02-26T15:24:46.212Z","summary":"## Goal\nFix AutoClaw browser automation skill configuration and connection issues, ensure compliance with OpenClaw skill build standards, create standardized documentation and scripts, and test complete functionality including bookmark creation and browser navigation.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Must follow OpenClaw configuration requirements (Gateway port 18789, token authentication, loopback binding)\n- Must adhere to industry-standard skill structure (SKILL.md, scripts/, examples/, etc.)\n- Must maintain compatibility with existing OpenClaw Gateway configuration\n- MCP server port must avoid conflicts with system services (originally 49667 conflicted with svchost.exe)\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Created comprehensive fix script (`fix_all_issues.js`) that verified and repaired MCP server, plugin background.js, options.js, manifest.json, and Gateway configuration\n- [x] Verified OpenClaw Gateway configuration compliance (port 18789, mode: local, bind: loopback, auth: token)\n- [x] Created OpenClaw configuration compliance check script (`openclaw_config_check.js`)\n- [x] Created optimized configuration guide (`autoclaw_optimized_config.md`)\n- [x] Analyzed skill structure against industry standards (compared with clawddocs-1.2.2)\n- [x] Created standard SKILL.md file with comprehensive documentation\n- [x] Created detailed README.md with installation, configuration, and usage instructions\n- [x] Created scripts directory with build and startup scripts for both bash and PowerShell\n- [x] Created examples directory with basic-usage.md containing practical examples\n- [x] Modified MCP server port from 49667 to 30000 due to port conflict with svchost.exe (EACCES: permission denied)\n- [x] Updated plugin configuration to use port 30000 instead of 18789 for direct MCP connection (new architecture)\n- [x] Successfully built and launched MCP server on port 30000 with WebSocket connectivity verified\n- [x] Tested and validated claw_create_folder tool: created \"today\" bookmark folder successfully (folder ID: 377, parentId: 2)\n- [x] Tested and validated claw_navigate tool: successfully sent navigation commands to https://tv.cctv.com/live and https://www.douyin.com\n- [x] Created functional test report (`D:\\工作报告\\20260226_02_AutoClaw功能测试_执行报告.md`) documenting all test results\n- [x] Identified and documented Chrome extension attachment behavior issue (controls GitHub tab instead of current active tab)\n- [x] Modified `background.js` to synchronize icon state with actual WebSocket status (global badge updates, error state handling, connection state tracking)\n- [x] Modified MCP server (`C:\\Users\\lenovo\\.openclaw\\skills\\claw-browser\\autoclaw-mcp\\src\\server.ts`) to check Gateway availability before WebSocket connection attempt\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Testing modified plugin after reloading extension\n- [ ] Resolving Chrome extension attachment behavior to control current active tab instead of background tabs\n- [ ] Testing automatic tab attachment configuration in extension options\n\n### Blocked\n- Chrome extension currently attaches to background GitHub tab (`https://github.com/`) instead of user's active tab, limiting usability\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Standardized skill structure**: Adopted industry-standard layout with SKILL.md, scripts/, and examples/ directories based on analysis of clawddocs-1.2.2\n- **Dual-platform scripts**: Created both bash (.sh) and PowerShell (.ps1) versions of build/start scripts for cross-platform compatibility\n- **Configuration compliance**: Ensured all configurations strictly follow OpenClaw Gateway requirements (port 18789, token auth, loopback binding)\n- **Port change decision**: Modified MCP server port from 49667 to 30000 to avoid conflict with system service (svchost.exe using 49667)\n- **Architecture upgrade**: Adopted new direct connection architecture (OpenClaw → MCP (30000) ← Chrome Extension → Browser) instead of routing through Gateway\n- **Modified icon state logic**: Changed from config-based to WebSocket connection-state-based to resolve UI/state mismatch\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Reload AutoClaw extension in Chrome (via `chrome://extensions`)\n2. Configure plugin with correct token (`Q0hpK2oV4F9tlwbYX3RELxiJNGDvayr8OPqZzkfs`) and port (30000)\n3. Verify icon now accurately shows connection state (ON/green when connected)\n4. Test browser automation commands to ensure full functionality\n5. Fix Chrome extension attachment behavior to control current active tab instead of background tabs\n6. Test automatic tab attachment configuration in extension options\n7. Add version management to package.json\n8. Create additional advanced usage examples\n9. Consider publishing to ClawdHub skill repository\n\n## Critical Context\n- OpenClaw Gateway configuration: \n  ```json\n  {\n    \"gateway\": {\n      \"port\": 18789,\n      \"mode\": \"local\",\n      \"bind\": \"loopback\",\n      \"auth\": {\n        \"mode\": \"token\",\n        \"token\": \"Q0hpK2oV4F9tlwbYX3RELxiJNGDvayr8OPqZzkfs\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  ```\n- MCP server now runs on port 30000 (changed from 49667 due to svchost.exe conflict)\n- Chrome extension connects directly to MCP server on port 30000 (new architecture)\n- All files located in `C:\\Users\\lenovo\\.openclaw\\skills\\claw-browser\\`\n- Chrome extension requires manual installation via `chrome://extensions` with developer mode enabled\n- Token encoding supports special characters through `encodeURIComponent`\n- Modified files: `C:\\Users\\lenovo\\.openclaw\\skills\\claw-browser\\autoclaw-plugin\\background.js` and `C:\\Users\\lenovo\\.openclaw\\skills\\claw-browser\\autoclaw-mcp\\src\\server.ts`\n- Test reports: `D:\\工作报告\\20260226_01_autoclaw功能测试_执行报告.md` and `D:\\工作报告\\20260226_02_AutoClaw功能测试_执行报告.md`\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n## Goal\n- Open all links in the \"N8N\" bookmark folder\n\